a stair up to the surface. after abour 100 searches it suggests that it has
created a bad level and that I ought to give up.  This assumes that I am
running this program in a xterm or aixterm that has been manually resized to
be larger than 80x24.  If I try to run it a second time in the same window,
the only key that the program will respond to is control-c. and after THAT
escape, I will not get keyboard echo or line-feeds bound to the return key.

Clearly something is wrong here.  Has anybody else run into and solved these
problems? I should note that I am using the tty-based i/o, as I suspect that
trying to compile in X support with AIXWindows would take more code-bashing
that I could stand.  I am linking with -lcurses and -ltermcap, if that makes 
any difference.  Anyway, I would appreciate hearing about solutions to these
problems that people have found.



